<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.edge.settles ~ the key side answers the fleet's raises, idempotent

`lares edge settle [--fleet <root>]` reads the raises this vessel counts on its fleet's edge board, has the daemon island answer them where the face's group keys live, and marks what got answered; running it again changes nothing. A vessel holding no face's root settles nothing and says so.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ settle · fleet

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`settle` params=`~ settle every fleet`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`fleet` params=`fleet/<root> ~ settle one fleet`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ fleet

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`fleet` params=`takes/root ~ the fleet root; absent, every fleet this vessel holds a face root for`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the daemon island answers where the face's group keys live`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ EdgeSeatError

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`EdgeSeatError` params=`~ the seat read or mark refused by name`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ settled · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`settled` params=`exit/0 ~ each fleet answered and marked, or nothing to settle`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`exit/1 ~ refused by name`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

